  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EBRD Ivano-Frankivsk District Heating - Ivano-Frankivsk DH Investment Grant</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EBRD Ivano-Frankivsk Fj&#xe4;rrv&#xe4;rm</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Fj&#xe4;rrv&#xe4;rmeinvestering i Ivano Frankivsk Ukriana. Sverige ha bidragit  med ett investeringsbidrag.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investment support to Ivano-Frankivsk  District Heating Project  in Ukraine. Sweden has contributed with an investment  grant.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ivano-Frankivsk District Heating Project addresses the urgent investments targeted at improving the energy efficiency as well as the quality of district heating service provision and reduced losses incurred in the distribution networks. The introduction of individual heating substations represents the first step investments at the customer demand side that will transfer control of heating from the supplier to the end-users. And biomass fueled boiler generates heat using carbon neutral energy source contributing to emission reductions.&#xa0;
The Sida investment grant of MSEK 41.5 is used to (i) co-finance purchasing of a 4MW biofuel boiler along with the auxiliary equipment at the Troleybusna boiler house, and (ii) finance up to 144 individual heat substations (&#x201c;IHSs&#x201d;) in the city of Ivano-Frankivsk in Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
